    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_component_type\",\n      \"components\": [\"U2\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U2.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\"],\n      \"observed\": \"PCA9685PW address pin A0 (pin 1) is tied to the +3.3V net, while the other address pins A1 to A5 (pins 2, 3, 4, 5, 24) are tied to GND. A0 at logic high sets address bit 0 to 1, so the device would answer at 0x41, not 0x40.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Per the specification, the PWM driver's I2C address is 0x40, which requires A0 to be tied to GND like the other address pins.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A0\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A1\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The FCC cannot communicate with the PWM/servo driver at the specified address, so servo outputs would not be driven as intended.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.6\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"L1\", \"REG2\", \"U2\", \"FCC1\", \"NAVC1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"REG2.1\", \"FCC1.28\", \"NAVC1.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\", \"+3V3\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The LDO output that the spec calls the 3V3 rail for MCUs and sensors is on net '+3.3V', but the MCU supply pins and MCU decoupling are on a separate net '+3V3'. No netlist connection joins the two nets, so the LDO output does not reach the MCU supply pins.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The 3.3 V LDO output should feed both MCUs and the sensors on a single 3.3 V rail.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"+3.3V\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"2\\\") (name \\\"+3V3\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) | ST LD39200PU33R\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the nets are not joined in the physical board, the MCUs would have no 3.3 V supply, and the board would not boot.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The strongest finding is that PCA9685 address pin A0 is tied to +3.3V instead of GND, which shifts the device address from the specified 0x40 to 0x41. A lower-confidence concern is that the LDO output and the MCU supply are on differently named nets with no joining connection, which may be a labelling artifact.\"\n}",
